 With Hyprland only, there is no protocol to parse: the built-in module and Hyprland's dispatchers should cover the whole table. Checked at step 1: `Hyprland.workspaces` (`id`, `name`, `active`, `focused`, `urgent`), `Hyprland.activeToplevel` and `Hyprland.toplevels` (`title`, `urgent`, `workspace`, and `appId` through the `wayland` handle), and `Hyprland.dispatch()`. Dispatcher syntax differs when `Hyprland.usingLua` is true.
 
@@ -74,7 +80,7 @@ Found at runtime in phase 2 (Hyprland 0.56.2, Lua config):
 - `Hyprland.toplevels` holds `HyprlandToplevel` objects, though the docs label it `Toplevel`. Their `activated` reads false for the focused window at startup; the `wayland` handle's `activated` is right.
 - The Hyprland, Networking and Bluetooth modules start empty and fill in a second or two after first use, so every binding must handle null and empty lists.
 
-**Auto-hide rule.** The bar hides when any window on the current workspace intersects the bar's rectangle plus a small margin. A thin always-present strip at the bottom edge shows it again on hover. For this to work the bar must not reserve screen space (exclusive zone 0). There is no bottom gap, so tiled windows overlap the bar as well and it stays hidden while the workspace has windows.
+**Auto-hide rule.** The bar hides when any window on the current workspace intersects the bar's rectangle plus a small margin. A thin always-present strip at the bottom edge shows it again on hover. For this to work the bar must not reserve screen space (exclusive zone 0). There is no bottom gap, so tiled windows overlap the bar as well and it stays hidden while the workspace has windows. While the focused window is fullscreen (`Compositor.fullscreen`, the Wayland toplevel's own state: Hyprland's maximized mode reads as `maximized`, not fullscreen, checked) the strip goes and the handle fades, so a stray pointer at the edge can't bring the bar up over a game (owner's request, after phase 8); a panel opened by keybind still shows it.
 
 ## Theme and motion
 
@@ -102,6 +108,7 @@ Motion rules, so everything feels the same:
 - Popups fade in and rise about 12 px. Panels grow from the chip that opened them.
 - The active workspace capsule animates its width between 8 and 26 px as focus moves.
 - The bar shrinks into its handle when it hides and grows out of it when it returns (owner's request, after phase 8; it used to slide down while fading): one 0–1 `grown` on the curve, over 300 ms (`Theme.growDuration`; the owner found 200 ms too quick for it), drives the pill's size, position and colour, from the 72 × 4 handle 2 px above the edge to the 640 × 56 pill, the handle's `subtext` giving way to `bgAlt` within the first third. The content sits apart at full size, since anchored chips would squash, and fades in rising 6 px over the second half (it goes first when hiding). The tray pill follows the same curve, budding out of its edge beside the bar.
+- The startup animation (owner's request, after phase 8): as the shell starts, the bar and its pills drop to the handle at once, the wallpaper fades in from `bg` over `Theme.introDuration` (600 ms), and once it has (or after 1.5 s without one) the bar grows out of its handle. A `PersistentProperties` in `shell.qml` (`started`, carried over a reload before its `loaded()`) keeps a live reload from playing it; `psc restart` does (checked with frames 100 ms apart).
 - Values ease instead of jumping (owner's request, after phase 8): `components/Slider.qml` draws an eased `shown` position (disabled while pressed, so a drag stays exact) and its `shownValue` lets the labels in quick settings and the launcher count along; the OSD's bar and number ease too, but start at the value while hidden or on a switch between volume and brightness.
 - The launcher's selection is one chip under the rows that glides between them, carrying the ↵ chip on result rows (owner's request; `ResultRow` leaves it room, and its action label fades in), so the two move together (the rows draw no selected background of their own; grid rows and questions keep marking their choice inside, so it fades out there); the mode tabs share one sliding chip. On opening, a mode switch and a power question, rows fade in rising 8 px, 20 ms apart, and the chip jumps instead of gliding (owner's request, after phase 8). A move within 100 ms of the last one also jumps: a held arrow repeats every 30 ms or so, and restarting the glide each time left the chip almost three rows behind the selection (measured). The chip is parented to the list's `contentItem` by hand: declared in the ListView it wasn't, so once the list scrolled it sat `contentY` off, on another row than the ↵ chip (the owner saw it).
 - Closing runs the opening motion backwards. Each window has an `open` flag and a `Reveal` (`components/Reveal.qml`) that eases a 0–1 `progress` and keeps the window up until the fade-out ends; content binds its opacity and scale or offset to that progress. Toasts fade out sinking 12 px when they expire or are dismissed. The lock screen's content fades in over its plain background.
